Body:
Adding another use case to support this request.

I have a project-level plugin (`.opencode/plugins/worktree.ts`) that creates a git worktree for each session on `session.created`. The worktrees are created correctly, but the session `directory` is always the repo root — so built-in tools like `bash`, `read`, and `edit` still run there instead of in the worktree.

What I'd like is a way to configure this in `opencode.json` so that every new session automatically gets its own worktree workspace and runs tools there. Something like:

```json
{
  "experimental": {
    "workspace": {
      "type": "worktree"
    }
  }
}
```

This would make the worktree the default execution context for all sessions in that project, without requiring manual workspace selection in the TUI each time.

@KochC i can second your findings, this was my first approach and I ran into the same limitations. As I understand it, you cant mutate the current active workdir from within a plugin, or at least it is not getting propagated to tools. I tried a different hook, but observation was as you just described.

```javascript
await Plugin.trigger("tool.execute.before", ..., { args: args3 });
const result = await item.execute(args3, ctx);
```

So if a plugin is able to change the current working directory in a running session, one could make the switch and build up custom workflows. It might also be, that this is intended to create immutable session runtime for stability / security concerns. However, then i would appreciate to be able to at least fork the session with respective runtime settings (e.g. a worktree path becoming the sessions working directory) adjusted for the tools. 

Then my above suggestions would even become obsolete :)
